Files:
goes_aia_validated.csv: Cleaned and cross-checked list of flares
	flare_id: Auto-generated flare identifier
	end_time: End-time of the flare
	event_date: Date of the flare
	goes_class: GOES class of the flare
	goes_location: GOES location of the flare
	noaa_active_region: Assigned AR number
	peak_time: peak time of the flare
	start_time: start time of the flare
	fl_location: location of the flare either reported by NOAA or approximated from AR centroids
	fl_lat: flare latitude component from  fl_location
	fl_lon: flare longitude component from  fl_location
	y: y-coordinate
	x: x-coordinate
	centroids: approximated AR centroid location
	x_hpc: HPC x coordinate
	y_hpc: HPC y coordinate
	ssw_dist: Distance to the closest AIA flare reported by SSW Latest Events module
	fd_dist: Distance to the closest AIA flare Flare Detective Module

invalidated_goes_final.csv: includes two sets of flare reports: (1) Flares without NOAA AR number and spatial location and (2) Flares that does not have a corresponding AIA flare.
	end_time: End-time of the flare
	event_date: Date of the flare
	goes_class: GOES class of the flare
	goes_location: GOES location of the flare
	noaa_active_region: Assigned AR number
	peak_time: peak time of the flare
	start_time: start time of the flare


fixed_all_xrs: integrated time series of X-ray flux
	Timestamp: time of the X-ray flux
	B_AVG: 1-min averaged X-ray flux integrated over multiple GOES missions

noaa_ars.csv: integrated daily NOAA AR data (SRS), relevant columns:
	noaa_ar_no: assigned NOAA AR number
	year, month, day: year, month, and date of the AR
	x, y: x and y coordinates of the NOAA ARs

all_harps_with_noaa_ars.txt: Matching between HARPNUMs and NOAA ARs as provided by JSOC/SHARP (separated with space character)
	col[0]: HARPNUM
	col[1]: a comma-separated list of associated NOAA AR numbers
